# Suite run (plan 04-06, D-08, A-06): run, observation, buffer and input tests through the public
# API, in their own executable (the 512-case machine suite and its per-fault reruns stay bounded).
# Family observe (plan 04-06): ivs_machine_cpu_state (OFF, after reset, after stepped units of
# stand-in program A, flag mapping, the out-struct size rule), ivs_machine_peek (loaded words, the
# 10-bit mask, closed gates and undriven space equal to a CPU read, the address-space end), side-
# effect freedom over 1000 peeks and 1000 cpu_state calls OFF and POWERED, and the refusals of both
# calls with the SP4 oracle (status, whole-storage memcmp, digests and machine time equal, poisoned
# out kept).
run.cpu-state.off
run.cpu-state.after-reset
run.cpu-state.after-steps
run.cpu-state.flag-bits
run.cpu-state.larger-struct
run.peek.loaded-words
run.peek.gated
run.peek.undriven
run.peek.after-steps
run.peek.range-end-ok
run.observe.no-side-effect-off
run.observe.no-side-effect-powered
run.refuse.cpu-state.null
run.refuse.cpu-state.struct-size
run.refuse.cpu-state.bad-handle
run.refuse.cpu-state.out-inside-instance
run.refuse.peek.null-out
run.refuse.peek.count-zero
run.refuse.peek.bad-handle
run.refuse.peek.out-inside-instance
run.refuse.peek.range-end
run.refuse.peek.range-before-overlap
# Family bound (plan 04-07, D-01..D-05): ivs_machine_run to an absolute master-tick target. The
# expected boundaries come from a reference twin stepped unit by unit through the internal seam;
# targets inside a unit, on a boundary and already reached; overshoot over a window of targets;
# run(now + 1) equals one seam step.
run.target.ends-at-first-boundary-ge-target
run.target.on-boundary-no-overshoot
run.target.already-reached
run.overshoot.equals-now-minus-target
run.single-step.equals-seam
